---
// /for-manufacturers — manufacturer-track audience landing page. Full 8-step
// storyboard end-to-end, CEO-as-protagonist register, with the designer-
// demand callout in the Insight section to surface the dual-track activation
// flywheel without diluting the manufacturer pitch.
//
// Spec:          docs/tasks/sections/for-manufacturers.md
// Copy:          docs/growth/copy/for-manufacturers.md
// Positioning:   docs/growth/positioning-manufacturer.md
// Storyboard:    docs/growth/sales-pitch-storyboard-manufacturer.md

import PageShell from '../components/PageShell.astro';
import StickyToc from '../components/StickyToc.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import CrossLinkFooter from '../components/CrossLinkFooter.astro';
import DiscoveryLoopDiagram from '../components/DiscoveryLoopDiagram.astro';
import ManufacturerFlowDiagram from '../components/ManufacturerFlowDiagram.astro';

const tocItems = [
  { href: '#insight', label: 'Where discovery is going' },
  { href: '#introduction', label: 'What ULC is' },
  { href: '#how-to-create', label: 'How to create' },
  { href: '#themes', label: 'Differentiated value' },
  { href: '#the-ask', label: 'The Ask' },
];

const crossLinks = [
  { href: '/validator', labelHtml: 'Try the validator on a candidate <code>.ulc</code> file' },
  { href: '/docs', labelHtml: 'Authoring patterns and PIM mapping guides' },
  { href: '/docs#how-to-use-today', labelHtml: 'Two-tier consumption deep dive' },
  { href: '/governance', labelHtml: 'Stewardship and open license' },
  { href: '/#adopters', labelHtml: 'See current adopters' },
  { href: '/for-designers', labelHtml: 'Demand side: the designer track' },
];

const pageTitle = 'ULC for luminaire manufacturers: the AI-discovery layer';
const pageDescription = 'Specifier discovery is shifting from PDF to AI-mediated. The manufacturers whose data is machine-readable are the ones AI surfaces. Pilot a publication.';
---

<PageShell title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
  {/* Hero band */}
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="dot-grid" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div
      class="relative mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 pt-16 pb-12 md:px-10 md:pt-24 md:pb-16 lg:pt-28 lg:pb-20"
    >
      <p class="small-caps text-xs md:text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)] mb-6">
        Manufacturer track
      </p>
      <h1
        class="hero-display max-w-5xl text-balance break-words font-display font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--text)] text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-[3.25rem] leading-[1.1]"
      >
        For lighting manufacturers
      </h1>
      <p
        class="mt-6 md:mt-8 max-w-3xl text-base md:text-lg lg:text-xl text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed"
      >
        Specifier discovery is shifting from PDF to AI-mediated. The manufacturers whose data is structured and machine-readable are the ones AI tools surface, the ones design tools consume natively, and the ones designers ask for by name.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* Body: 2-col on desktop with sticky TOC sidebar, single-col on mobile */}
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 md:px-10 pb-24 lg:grid lg:grid-cols-[16rem_minmax(0,1fr)] lg:gap-12">
    <div class="lg:pt-12">
      <StickyToc items={tocItems} />
    </div>

    <article class="long-form pt-10 lg:pt-12 max-w-[68ch]">

      {/* ── 1. INSIGHT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
      <section id="insight" aria-labelledby="insight-heading">
        <p class="step-num">Step 1</p>
        <h2 id="insight-heading">Where specifier discovery is going</h2>
        <p>
          Specifier discovery is moving from the designer opening a PDF to the designer asking an AI which luminaire fits a project. The manufacturers whose data is machine-readable are the ones that surface. Eventually, the ones that get the usage telemetry back. The bottleneck for that whole loop is not the AI. It is the data layer underneath, which today is PDF.
        </p>
        <DiscoveryLoopDiagram />

        <Callout intent="accent" label="Designer demand, in motion">
          <p>
            Designers are starting to ask their preferred manufacturer reps for ULC files. The activation flywheel turns through designer-to-rep advocacy. The demand-side surface is at <a href="/for-designers" class="link-inline">/for-designers</a>.
          </p>
        </Callout>

        <p>
          The bottleneck is solvable today with structured publishing, ahead of the analytics loop that does not yet exist. The first manufacturers to publish are the ones the industry remembers as having defined the layer.
        </p>
      </section>

      {/* ── 4. INTRODUCTION ────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
      <section id="introduction" aria-labelledby="introduction-heading">
        <p class="step-num">Step 4</p>
        <h2 id="introduction-heading">What ULC is</h2>
        <p>
          ULC is the open standard for luminaire product data. The machine-readable layer AI tools, design tools, and spec databases read alongside your existing PDF, IES, and LDT.
        </p>
        <ManufacturerFlowDiagram />
        <p>
          Today, you publish PDF + IES + LDT separately. An extraction layer (AI tool or aggregator pipeline) tries to read structure from your PDF, lossy. An aggregator or spec database re-publishes its interpretation. The designer's tool consumes the aggregator's interpretation, with errors.
        </p>
        <p>
          With ULC, you publish PDF + IES + LDT + a ULC record. Source files are referenced by SHA-256 hash, not embedded. The designer's AI or design tool fetches your ULC record directly, verifies the hash, parses native JSON.
        </p>
        <Callout intent="default" label="What ULC replaces vs integrates with">
          <p>
            ULC does not replace your PDF, your IES, your LDT, your rep agency, your distributor, your existing PIM, or any existing commercial relationship. It integrates with your existing PIM via the published mapping guides (Salsify, Akeneo, SAP, custom).
          </p>
          <p>
            What it replaces is the aggregator's interpretation as the data layer the designer's tool actually reads. The aggregator can still exist; it is no longer the authoritative source.
          </p>
        </Callout>
      </section>

      {/* ── 5. HOW TO CREATE A ULC FILE ────────────────────────────────── */}
      <section id="how-to-create" aria-labelledby="how-to-create-heading">
        <p class="step-num">Authoring</p>
        <h2 id="how-to-create-heading">How to create a ULC file</h2>
        <p>
          A <code>.ulc</code> file is JSON, validated against an open schema, and references your existing PDF, IES, and LDT files by SHA-256 hash, not embedded. The schema defines the structural shape: required fields, types, and nested blocks like <code>sources[]</code> for hash-referenced source files, <code>applicability[]</code> for configurator axes, and <code>provenance[]</code> for per-IES models. The taxonomy defines the value-sets: enumerated CCT brackets, CRI bands, beam angles, IP ratings, optic types, mounting categories. Together they make every meaningful product attribute machine-comparable across manufacturers.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Path A: Map from your PIM.</strong> If your product data lives in Salsify, Akeneo, SAP Product Master, or a custom PIM system, the structured data already exists. The authoring-patterns and PIM-mapping guides at <a href="/docs" class="link-inline">/docs</a> walk through field-by-field translation from each PIM schema to the ULC schema. Most of the lift is mapping your internal field names and value-sets onto ULC's canonical fields and taxonomy. The mapping is typically a one-time integration; <code>.ulc</code> generation then runs as part of your existing publishing pipeline.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Path B: Convert from PDF, IES, and LDT.</strong> If your authoritative product data still lives in cutsheets and photometric files, you can author <code>.ulc</code> records by hand or with LLM assistance using the schema as a contract. The four canonical example records in <a href="https://github.com/ulcspec/ULC/tree/main/examples" target="_blank" rel="noopener external" class="link-inline">ulcspec/ULC/examples/</a> are templates covering the four authoring patterns: single-SKU cutsheet, configurator with applicability blocks, per-IES with provenance classes, and per-foot linear scaling. Open a sample, replace the manufacturer, product, and SKU fields with yours, populate the photometric and electrical values from your existing cutsheets, and reference your source files by URL plus SHA-256 hash.
        </p>
        <p>
          The schema source of truth lives at <a href="https://github.com/ulcspec/ULC" target="_blank" rel="noopener external" class="link-inline">github.com/ulcspec/ULC</a>: the <a href="https://github.com/ulcspec/ULC/tree/main/schema" target="_blank" rel="noopener external" class="link-inline">JSON Schema and taxonomy</a>, the <a href="https://github.com/ulcspec/ULC/tree/main/examples" target="_blank" rel="noopener external" class="link-inline">four example records</a>, and the <a href="https://github.com/ulcspec/ULC/tree/main/mappings" target="_blank" rel="noopener external" class="link-inline">PIM mapping guides</a>. The <a href="/validator" class="link-inline">validator</a> catches schema errors at upload before publication; it runs the same validation as the upstream repo's CI. The full authoring-pattern deep dives, taxonomy reference, and crosswalks live at <a href="/docs" class="link-inline">/docs</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      {/* ── 6. WHAT DIFFERENCE A ULC FILE MAKES (3 bullets) ────────────── */}
      <section id="themes" aria-labelledby="themes-heading">
        <p class="step-num">Step 5</p>
        <h2 id="themes-heading">What difference a ULC file makes</h2>
        <p>
          ULC turns your product data into a layer AI tools, design tools, and spec databases consume natively. Three concrete shifts.
        </p>

        <ul class="value-list">
          <li>
            <strong>Found in AI-mediated specifier discovery with correct attributes.</strong> When a designer asks an AI which 2700K downlight under 40W fits a project, your products are in the answer set with the right CCT, CRI, optical accessories, and IP rating, sourced from you, not whatever the extraction layer guessed off your PDF.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Direct data channel from you to the designer's tool, hash-verifiable.</strong> The designer's AI agent, design tool, and spec database fetch your authoritative <code>.ulc</code> record from your infrastructure, verify it against your source files by SHA-256 hash, and parse it natively. No aggregator's interpretation sitting in the middle. Your rep, distributor, and aggregator relationships stay where they are.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Early-mover position in the standard your peers will adopt.</strong> Open, MIT-licensed, neutrally stewarded, with active dialogue with DIAL, LIA, and IES, and pilot conversations underway. The first manufacturers to publish are the ones the industry remembers as having defined the layer.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      {/* ── 7. THE ASK ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
      <section id="the-ask" aria-labelledby="the-ask-heading">
        <p class="step-num">Step 6</p>
        <h2 id="the-ask-heading">The Ask</h2>
        <p>
          ULC is a new open-source standard. The activation mechanic turns when forward-leaning manufacturers pilot the publication shape and tell us what breaks.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Ask is one specific commitment: pilot 1-3 SKUs as <code>.ulc</code> files in the next 90 days. The lowest-cost path is one product line at a time. The four canonical example records show what a finished <code>.ulc</code> looks like across the authoring patterns. The validator catches the easy issues. The conversations that follow shape what the standard becomes.
        </p>
        <p>
          Open an issue, contribute, or browse the schema and example records on <a
            href="https://github.com/ulcspec/ULC"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener external"
          >GitHub</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

    </article>
  </div>

  <CrossLinkFooter links={crossLinks} />
</PageShell>

<style>
  /* ── Long-form prose, manufacturer-document register ─────────────────
     Matches /for-designers' .long-form so the two audience surfaces share
     a single prose token system. Any change here must land on /for-designers
     too; the next long-form surface (/docs) consolidates these as
     prose-* tokens in DESIGN_SYSTEM.md (deferred to PR-A2 per
     for-designers-plan §10.4). */
  .long-form {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .long-form > section {
    margin-top: 4.5rem;
    scroll-margin-top: 5rem;
  }
  .long-form > section:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .long-form p {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem 0;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
  .long-form p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .long-form strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .long-form code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.95em;
    color: var(--accent-warm);
  }
  .long-form a {
    color: var(--accent-warm);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .long-form a:hover {
    color: var(--accent-warm-deep);
  }

  .step-num {
    font-variant-caps: all-small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-subtle);
    margin: 0 0 0.625rem 0 !important;
  }

  .long-form h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 1.875rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem 0;
    max-width: 28ch;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .long-form h2 {
      font-size: 2.25rem;
    }
  }
  .long-form h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0.75rem 0;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .long-form h3 {
      font-size: 1.375rem;
    }
  }

  /* ── Alternatives table ───────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .alt-table {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
    display: block;
  }
  .alt-table thead,
  .alt-table tbody,
  .alt-table tr {
    display: block;
  }
  .alt-table thead {
    display: none;
  }
  .alt-table tr {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 1rem 1.125rem;
  }
  .alt-table tr:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }
  .alt-table th[scope='row'],
  .alt-table td {
    display: block;
    text-align: left;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .alt-table th[scope='row'] {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }
  .alt-table td + td {
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .alt-table {
      display: table;
    }
    .alt-table thead {
      display: table-header-group;
      background: var(--bg);
    }
    .alt-table tbody {
      display: table-row-group;
    }
    .alt-table tr {
      display: table-row;
      padding: 0;
    }
    .alt-table th,
    .alt-table td {
      display: table-cell;
      padding: 1.125rem 1.25rem;
      vertical-align: top;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .alt-table tr:last-child th,
    .alt-table tr:last-child td {
      border-bottom: none;
    }
    .alt-table th[scope='col'] {
      font-variant-caps: all-small-caps;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      color: var(--text-subtle);
      text-align: left;
      font-weight: 500;
    }
    .alt-table th[scope='row'] {
      margin-bottom: 0;
      width: 30%;
    }
    .alt-table td + td {
      margin-top: 0;
    }
  }
  /* Companion row (the ULC fifth row) — matches sibling /for-designers
     neutral 4% mix so the two surfaces share one alt-table treatment.
     The accent-warm row header keeps the ULC name highlighted without
     repainting the whole row. */
  .alt-table .alt-row--companion {
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--text-subtle) 4%, var(--bg-elevated));
  }
  .alt-table .alt-row--companion th[scope='row'] {
    color: var(--accent-warm);
  }

  /* ── Criteria list ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .criteria-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    counter-reset: criterion;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .criteria-list > li {
    counter-increment: criterion;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-warm);
    padding: 0.125rem 0 0.125rem 1.25rem;
    position: relative;
  }
  .criteria-list > li::before {
    content: counter(criterion, decimal-leading-zero);
    position: absolute;
    left: -2.5rem;
    top: 0.25rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-subtle);
    display: none;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .criteria-list > li {
      padding-left: 1.5rem;
    }
    .criteria-list > li::before {
      display: block;
    }
    .criteria-list {
      padding-left: 2.5rem;
    }
  }
  .criteria-list h3 {
    margin-top: 0;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .criteria-list h3 {
      font-size: 1.125rem;
    }
  }
  .criteria-list p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin: 0.375rem 0 0 0;
  }

  /* ── Theme blocks (3) ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .theme {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 2.5rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem !important;
    scroll-margin-top: 5rem;
  }
  .theme:first-of-type {
    border-top: none;
    padding-top: 0;
  }
  .theme__num {
    font-variant-caps: all-small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--accent-warm);
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0 !important;
  }
  .theme h3 {
    margin-top: 0;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
    max-width: 32ch;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .theme h3 {
      font-size: 1.625rem;
    }
  }
  .theme .return-line {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-warm);
    padding-left: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  /* ── Theme 1 extraction-vs-ULC contrast block ────────────────────── */
  .contrast {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .contrast {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
    }
  }
  .contrast__col {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    padding: 1rem 1.125rem;
  }
  .contrast__col--gain {
    border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent-warm) 35%, var(--border));
  }
  .contrast__label {
    font-variant-caps: all-small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    color: var(--text-subtle);
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
  }
  .contrast__col--gain .contrast__label {
    color: var(--accent-warm);
  }
  .contrast__list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.375rem;
  }
  .contrast__list li {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.45;
    padding-left: 0.875rem;
    position: relative;
  }
  .contrast__list li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.5rem;
    width: 4px;
    height: 4px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--text-subtle);
  }
  .contrast__col--gain .contrast__list li::before {
    background: var(--accent-warm);
  }
  .contrast-note {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    margin-top: 0.875rem !important;
  }

  /* ── Sources block code fragment ───────────────────────────────────── */
  .code-block {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    background: var(--code-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1rem 1.125rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--code-text);
  }
  .code-block code {
    font-family: inherit;
    color: inherit;
    font-size: inherit;
  }

  /* ── Inline dialogue strip (Theme 3) ───────────────────────────────
     In-column variant of the full-width DialogueStrip.astro (which is a
     <section>, can't drop inside an article column without breaking the
     68ch max-width). Single bottom rule + tighter letter-spacing reads as
     an "industry beat" inside flowing prose, not a horizontal-rule pair. */
  .dialogue-strip {
    margin-top: 1.5rem !important;
    padding: 0.625rem 1.125rem 0.875rem;
    text-align: center;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-variant-caps: all-small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.10em;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .dialogue-strip strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .dialogue-strip span {
    color: var(--text-subtle);
    margin: 0 0.5rem;
  }

  /* ── Link variants ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .link {
    color: var(--accent-warm);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.25rem;
    min-height: 44px;
    padding: 0.375rem 0;
  }
  .link:hover {
    color: var(--accent-warm-deep);
  }
  /* Inline anchor inside flowing prose (does not need 44px touch target;
     the parent line already has hit-area). */
  .link-inline {
    color: var(--accent-warm);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .link-inline:hover {
    color: var(--accent-warm-deep);
  }

  /* ── Differentiated-value bullets ──────────────────────────────────
     Mirrors src/pages/for-designers.astro `.value-list`. Keep the two in
     sync until a shared prose token system lands per DESIGN_SYSTEM.md. */
  .value-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }
  .value-list > li {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-warm);
    padding: 0.125rem 0 0.125rem 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
  .value-list > li strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* ── Sample-link (matches /for-designers Try-ULC-today extra) ──────── */
  .sample-link {
    margin-top: 1.25rem !important;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
  .sample-link a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.375rem;
  }

  /* ── Proof matrix ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .proof-table {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    display: block;
  }
  .proof-table thead,
  .proof-table tbody,
  .proof-table tr {
    display: block;
  }
  .proof-table thead {
    display: none;
  }
  .proof-table tr {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
